The `processIntegers` function simply calls the `manageSharedResource` function to perform the main processing task. In this example, I've used a buffer size of 1024 for reading input from standard input, but you can adjust this value based on your specific requirements or constraints. This code demonstrates efficient memory management, scalability, and maintainability while considering potential integration with other systems or services.']

