The get_record() function returns a Record* that corresponds to the given offset, or null if no such record exists and the array needs resizing. It handles edge cases by checking if the offset is within the bounds of the current records array and adjusting the array size as needed. To address potential overflow conditions when setting random values within specified ranges, the function initializes all records with default values before use.

