        records[i].offset = offsets + keys[i];
        *records[i].offset = i;
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
    }

    gc(); // Initial garbage collection

    return records;
}

// Function to free the allocated memory
void cleanup() {
    size_t i;
    if (records != NULL) {
        munmap(records, num_keys * sizeof(record));
    }
    pthread_mutex_destroy(&mutex);
}
```

This code includes functions for initializing and cleaning up the data structures, as well as custom allocators for the offsets and records. It also incorporates a simple garbage collection mechanism, thread safety, and error handling. However, further optimizations such as lock-free data structures, memory pooling, performance-focused logging, and resource management are not included in this implementation.']

