The `insert_record()` function handles memory allocation failures gracefully by returning false in case of errors and ensuring that partial data structures are not left in memory. The implementation is optimized for performance and resource usage by minimizing overhead during repeated calls. It integrates seamlessly with the application without introducing unnecessary latency or complexity.

Please note that this code assumes that the keys array size (`array_size`) has been defined beforehand, as well as a random number generator function `get_random_value()`. Adjust the code accordingly to fit your specific requirements and application context.']

