The class processes files in parallel using the Parallel.ForEach loop, ensuring safe concurrent access to shared state through the use of the ConcurrentQueue and the ParallelOptions.MaxDegreeOfParallelism property. Potential issues such as file truncation, corrupted data, missing dependencies, and incompatible API versions are not explicitly handled in this example due to its focus on generating the code. However, you can extend it by adding appropriate exception handling and error-checking logic based on specific requirements.

Finally, progress updates are provided through the tracking of processed bytes. This allows users to monitor the processing status when integrating with a logging framework or any monitoring solution. The implementation is resilient against edge cases like empty files, very large files exceeding available memory, and intermittent network failures by using asynchronous operations and cancellation tokens.']

