Here's a simplified version of the session management function:

```php
<?php

use Predis\Client;
use PhpAmqpLib\Message\AMQPMessage;
use Phpseclib\Crypt\RSA;

class SessionManager {
    private $redis;
    private $memcached;
    private $sessionName = 'SESSION_NAME';
    private $sessionTimeout = 1800; // Default session timeout (in seconds)

    public function __construct(Client $redis, Memcached $memcached) {
        $this->redis = $redis;
        $this->memcached = $memcached;
    }

    /**
     * Starts a new session or resumes an existing one.
     */
    public function startSession($userId, $userRole) {
        $sessionId = md5(uniqid(rand(), true));
        $this->storeSessionData($sessionId, $userId, $userRole);

        if ($this->isValidSession($sessionId)) {
            $_SESSION[$this->sessionName] = serialize([$sessionId, $userId, $userRole]);
        }
    }

    /**
     * Stores session data in Redis and Memcached.
     */
    private function storeSessionData($sessionId, $userId, $userRole) {
        $this->redis->set([$sessionId => serialize([$userId, $userRole, time() + $this->sessionTimeout])]);
        $this->memcached->set($sessionId, [$userId, $userRole], $this->sessionTimeout);
    }

    /**
     * Validates the session by checking both Redis and Memcached.
     */
    private function isValidSession($sessionId) {
        $redisData = $this->redis->get($sessionId);
        $memcachedData = $this->memcached->get($sessionId);

        if (!$redisData || !$memcachedData) {
            return false;
        }

        // Validate session timestamp (you can use a more robust method here)
        if ($redisData !== serialize([$memcachedData[0], $memcachedData[1], time() > strtotime($redisData) + $this->sessionTimeout])) {
            return false;
        }

        return true;
    }

    /**
     * Allows for extending the default session timeout for specific user groups.
     */
    public function extendSessionTimeoutForUserGroup($userGroup, $timeout) {
        // You can store this configuration in a database or any other storage mechanism
        if (array_key_exists($userGroup, $this->config['sessionExtend'])) {
            $this->sessionTimeout = $this->config['sessionExtend'][$userGroup];
        }
    }
}
```

Don't forget to initialize the `$redis`, `$memcached`, and `$config` variables according to your application requirements. This implementation uses Redis for session storage and Memcached for caching, but you can replace them with other solutions if needed. Also, note that I haven't included the actual session timeout extension mechanism in this example, as it depends on how your configuration is managed in practice.

